@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Developer Reflection";
}

<div class="container mt-5">
    <div class="row justify-content-center">
        <div class="col-lg-10">
            <div class="card shadow-lg rounded-lg">
                <div class="card-header text-white text-center py-4">
                    <h1 class="mb-0"><i class="fas fa-code me-3"></i>Developer Reflection</h1>
                    <p class="mb-0 mt-2">A Journey Through ASP.NET Core Development</p>
                </div>
                <div class="card-body p-5">
                    
                    <div class="mb-5">
                        <h2 class="text-primary mb-4"><i class="fas fa-lightbulb me-2"></i>Project Overview</h2>
                        <p class="lead">
                            This ASP.NET Core application represents a comprehensive gradesheet management system that I developed 
                            to help educators track and manage student activities and grades efficiently.
                        </p>
                        <p>
                            The application features a modern maroon and grey color scheme, implements partial views for better code 
                            organization, and provides a clean, user-friendly interface for managing academic records.
                        </p>
                    </div>

                    <div class="mb-5">
                        <h2 class="text-primary mb-4"><i class="fas fa-tools me-2"></i>Technical Implementation</h2>
                        <h4 class="text-secondary mb-3">Architecture Choices</h4>
                        <ul class="list-group list-group-flush mb-4">
                            <li class="list-group-item"><strong>MVC Pattern:</strong> Utilized ASP.NET Core MVC architecture for clear separation of concerns</li>
                            <li class="list-group-item"><strong>Entity Framework:</strong> Implemented for database operations with a code-first approach</li>
                            <li class="list-group-item"><strong>Partial Views:</strong> Extracted reusable components for better maintainability</li>
                            <li class="list-group-item"><strong>JavaScript Separation:</strong> Moved view-specific JavaScript to dedicated files for better organization</li>
                        </ul>

                        <h4 class="text-secondary mb-3">Key Features Implemented</h4>
                        <div class="row">
                            <div class="col-md-6">
                                <ul class="list-group list-group-flush">
                                    <li class="list-group-item">CSV Import functionality</li>
                                    <li class="list-group-item">Advanced filtering and search</li>
                                    <li class="list-group-item">Student profile management</li>
                                    <li class="list-group-item">Activity tracking and editing</li>
                                </ul>
                            </div>
                            <div class="col-md-6">
                                <ul class="list-group list-group-flush">
                                    <li class="list-group-item">Bulk operations for missing activities</li>
                                    <li class="list-group-item">Responsive design with Bootstrap</li>
                                    <li class="list-group-item">Toast notifications for user feedback</li>
                                    <li class="list-group-item">Pagination for large datasets</li>
                                </ul>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>

                    <div class="mb-5">
                        <h2 class="text-primary mb-4"><i class="fas fa-palette me-2"></i>Design and User Experience</h2>
                        <p>
                            One of the most significant changes I made was implementing a warm, vintage brownish color scheme 
                            throughout the application. This created a nostalgic, sophisticated interface that evokes 
                            classic elegance compared to modern flat designs.
                        </p>
                        <div class="row mt-4">
                            <div class="col-md-4 text-center mb-3">
                                <div class="p-3 rounded" style="background: linear-gradient(135deg, #8B4513, #A0522D); color: #F5F2E8;">
                                    <h5>Primary Brown</h5>
                                    <code>#8B4513 → #A0522D</code>
                                </div>
                            </div>
                            <div class="col-md-4 text-center mb-3">
                                <div class="p-3 rounded" style="background-color: #D2B48C; color: #3C2E26;">
                                    <h5>Vintage Tan</h5>
                                    <code>#D2B48C</code>
                                </div>
                            </div>
                            <div class="col-md-4 text-center mb-3">
                                <div class="p-3 rounded" style="background-color: #F5F2E8; color: #3C2E26; border: 2px solid #D2B48C;">
                                    <h5>Vintage Cream</h5>
                                    <code>#F5F2E8</code>
                                </div>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>

                    <div class="mb-5">
                        <h2 class="text-primary mb-4"><i class="fas fa-code-branch me-2"></i>Code Organization Improvements</h2>
                        <p>
                            A major focus of this iteration was improving code organization and maintainability:
                        </p>
                        <div class="card mb-3">
                            <div class="card-header">
                                <h5 class="mb-0">Partial Views Implementation</h5>
                            </div>
                            <div class="card-body">
                                <ul>
                                    <li><strong>_EditActivityModalPartial.cshtml:</strong> Extracted the complex modal logic for activity editing</li>
                                    <li><strong>_StudentProfileFormsPartial.cshtml:</strong> Separated filter and bulk add forms for reusability</li>
                                </ul>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                        <div class="card mb-3">
                            <div class="card-header">
                                <h5 class="mb-0">JavaScript Modularization</h5>
                            </div>
                            <div class="card-body">
                                <ul>
                                    <li><strong>index.js:</strong> Form validation logic for CSV upload</li>
                                    <li><strong>records.js:</strong> Collapse functionality and tooltip initialization</li>
                                    <li><strong>studentProfile.js:</strong> Complex modal and AJAX functionality</li>
                                </ul>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>

                    <div class="mb-5">
                        <h2 class="text-primary mb-4"><i class="fas fa-chart-line me-2"></i>Challenges and Solutions</h2>
                        <div class="row">
                            <div class="col-md-6">
                                <div class="card h-100">
                                    <div class="card-header bg-warning text-dark">
                                        <h5 class="mb-0">Challenges Faced</h5>
                                    </div>
                                    <div class="card-body">
                                        <ul>
                                            <li>Managing complex state in modal dialogs</li>
                                            <li>Ensuring consistent styling across components</li>
                                            <li>Implementing efficient data filtering</li>
                                            <li>Handling AJAX form submissions</li>
                                        </ul>
                                    </div>
                                </div>
                            </div>
                            <div class="col-md-6">
                                <div class="card h-100">
                                    <div class="card-header bg-success text-white">
                                        <h5 class="mb-0">Solutions Implemented</h5>
                                    </div>
                                    <div class="card-body">
                                        <ul>
                                            <li>Extracted JavaScript into modular files</li>
                                            <li>Created comprehensive CSS variables</li>
                                            <li>Implemented server-side pagination</li>
                                            <li>Used modern async/await patterns</li>
                                        </ul>
                                    </div>
                                </div>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>

                    <div class="mb-5">
                        <h2 class="text-primary mb-4"><i class="fas fa-rocket me-2"></i>Key Learnings</h2>
                        <div class="alert alert-info">
                            <h5 class="alert-heading">Technical Insights</h5>
                            <ul class="mb-0">
                                <li>The importance of consistent code organization from the beginning of a project</li>
                                <li>How partial views can significantly improve maintainability in complex applications</li>
                                <li>The value of separating JavaScript concerns for better debugging and maintenance</li>
                                <li>How proper CSS architecture can enhance the entire user experience</li>
                            </ul>
                        </div>
                    </div>

                    <div class="mb-4">
                        <h2 class="text-primary mb-4"><i class="fas fa-future me-2"></i>Future Enhancements</h2>
                        <p>
                            Looking forward, there are several areas where this application could be further improved:
                        </p>
                        <div class="row">
                            <div class="col-md-12">
                                <ul class="list-group">
                                    <li class="list-group-item">
                                        <strong>Performance Optimization:</strong> Implement caching strategies for frequently accessed data
                                    </li>
                                    <li class="list-group-item">
                                        <strong>Authentication & Authorization:</strong> Add user management and role-based access control
                                    </li>
                                    <li class="list-group-item">
                                        <strong>API Development:</strong> Create REST API endpoints for mobile application integration
                                    </li>
                                    <li class="list-group-item">
                                        <strong>Advanced Analytics:</strong> Implement reporting and analytics dashboard for grade trends
                                    </li>
                                    <li class="list-group-item">
                                        <strong>Real-time Updates:</strong> Add SignalR for real-time notifications and updates
                                    </li>
                                </ul>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>

                </div>
                <div class="card-footer text-center py-4">
                    <p class="mb-2"><strong>Developed by:</strong> Francine Obis</p>
                    <p class="mb-0 text-muted">ASP.NET Core MVC Application - Midterm Laboratory Activity</p>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="text-center mt-5">
        <a asp-controller="Home" asp-action="Records" class="btn btn-primary btn-lg">
            <i class="fas fa-arrow-left me-2"></i> Back to Application
        </a>
    </div>
</div>
